WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:04.366
We were asked to help a global bank customer

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:08.199
that had spent two years developing an application

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.566
meant to be used by their tellers across their bank branches.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:18.266
That thousands of business users across hundreds of branches

00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:22.399
worldwide, were seeing performance problems.

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:32.466
When the customer has a problem, even though it's in code that they wrote

00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:34.099
that's still on top of our product

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.333
so we certainly jump in and help. 

00:00:36.566 --> 00:00:43.832
There were a lot of issues, and they escalated to our team, the SWAT Team

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:46.999
to come in and give an assist.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.233
Digital Business Automation SWAT Team is a little like a real SWAT team

00:00:54.233 --> 00:01:03.933
we're a quick response, reactive team that brings deep technical skills across all of our products 

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:07.466
to solve the customer's issue as quickly as possible.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.800
Any customer that's experiencing a difficult issue has access to the SWAT Team.

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:19.399
What we’re looking for is to really dig down into the problem

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.566
and get real, hands-on information to see

00:01:24.566 --> 00:01:29.799
where we can help and what we can do to best help the customer.

00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:36.532
You start when the customer starts, and you don't finish until the customer is done for the day.

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:41.566
So, it might be a 12-hour or a 16-hour day, it's whatever it takes.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.766
A problem like this, it's important to look at the entirety of the application.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.666
We want to look at the hardware it's running on

00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:53.032
we want to look at the operating system they're using

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:57.033
the database, and how they've developed their UI.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:02.566
And it was important for our team to come in and we were able to get them down to five seconds.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:09.666
One of the great things about working in IBM Support is every customer situation brings a new problem.

00:02:09.966 --> 00:02:12.866
And I know, based on our experience, that

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:16.866
we're going to solve that problem and we're going to get the customer to where they want to be. 

